    "description": "This lot contains a large assortment of loose gemstones and beads totaling 10.59 pounds. The collection includes a variety of natural stones, minerals, and shell pieces in multiple shapes, colors, and finishes such as polished, faceted, and raw. Some stones are strung as beads while others are loose, featuring materials like agate, quartz, malachite, lapis lazuli, shell, and glass. The mix offers a diverse range of textures and appearances within a single lot.\nPlease Note\nGemstones are tested using a Presidium Gem Tester. This tester cannot differentiate between manufactured and natural stones.\nGram weight includes materials and components of the entire item including stones unless noted.\nRefer to photos for any additional markings that may be present.\nHigh-end designer items are authenticated before listing.\nExpect items to have normal wear from use. Items may require cleaning.\nJewelry pieces present in collection lots may have unspecified minor flaws.\nDescriptions are made by individuals who may not have expertise specific to this type of item, in consultation with local and Internet resources. Shoppers are cautioned to evaluate items based upon their own resources. No guarantee of authenticity is implied unless specifically stated.\nHow Photography Affects Size Perception\nMacro (extreme close-up) photography is heavily utilized in jewelry listings, enabling viewers to examine pieces in larger-than-life detail. An accurate understanding of the actual sizes of these pieces cannot be deduced using photos alone. It is important that the bidder takes close note of the measurements and weights to determine actual sizes.\nAbout Gemstone & Metal Testing\nGemstones are tested with a Presidium Gem Tester. Goodwill of the Olympics & Rainier Region is a member of the International Gem Society; however, as we are not certified gemologists, we cannot guarantee the authenticity of any gemstone unless otherwise stated. Gemstone identification information is provided for your reference and consideration in bidding; no guarantee is implied.\nPearls are tested with a check for grittiness to detect nacre irregularities. We are generally unable to specify pearl types and characteristics; they may be cultured, wild, freshwater or saltwater pearls. Coral may be natural or dyed; most of our coral listings include dyed pieces.\nMetals including Gold, Silver, and Platinum are tested using an XRF precious metal analyzer, the Niton XL2 by Thermo Scientific, unless explicitly noted otherwise. XRF (X-ray fluorescence) analysis is a non-destructive testing method able to determine an item's elemental composition. Identification of other non-magnetic metals, including brass, bronze, copper, tin, and titanium, rely on our best estimation, and no guarantee is implied; they have not been tested or positively identified unless explicitly noted otherwise. Some jewelry may contain non-precious metals in clasps or findings, causing parts of the piece to respond to a magnet.\nCollections\nWe are not able to answer questions about or provide condition descriptions for specific pieces present in collections of jewelry sold for jewelry making and crafting purposes, or in grab bags. Many pieces have unspecified condition issues. Please view provided photographs to determine general contents. No part of such groupings may be returned for any reason.\nCondition descriptions for pieces present in scrap lots are not available and many pieces may have unspecified condition issues. Flaws may include missing stones, broken clasps, broken chains, bent or dented metal, repairs, and other damage. We are not able to answer questions about or provide condition descriptions for specific pieces present in scrap lots.\nAll items are sold as-is.",
